1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,227
Could someone place all these pictures
on

2
00:00:02,227 --> 00:00:05,355
a handmade Neocities page by writing
code?

3
00:00:05,355 --> 00:00:07,401
Let's look at one choice the maker

4
00:00:07,401 --> 00:00:08,720
actually made.

5
00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:10,824
The snail goes beside the note when

6
00:00:10,824 --> 00:00:11,986
there is room.

7
00:00:11,986 --> 00:00:14,782
This little stamp is another picture,
attached

8
00:00:14,782 --> 00:00:16,244
to the postcard.

9
00:00:16,244 --> 00:00:18,654
Both screens use the same files.

10
00:00:19,004 --> 00:00:21,348
Before we resize: what do you think

11
00:00:21,348 --> 00:00:23,166
will happen to the snail and the

12
00:00:23,166 --> 00:00:24,819
note on a narrow screen?

13
00:00:25,169 --> 00:00:26,387
Let's narrow it.

14
00:00:26,387 --> 00:00:28,938
Now the note stacks below the picture.

15
00:00:28,938 --> 00:00:31,293
The same rules keep the stamp attached

16
00:00:31,293 --> 00:00:32,636
to the postcard.

17
00:00:32,986 --> 00:00:36,344
A PNG screenshot freezes layout and
text.

18
00:00:36,344 --> 00:00:38,546
An SVG can stay crisp and may

19
00:00:38,546 --> 00:00:41,731
contain selectable text, but scaling a
fixed

20
00:00:41,731 --> 00:00:44,273
composition is not the same as HTML

21
00:00:44,273 --> 00:00:45,205
reflowing.

22
00:00:45,555 --> 00:00:47,796
Start in a plain text editor.

23
00:00:47,796 --> 00:00:50,226
Save index dot html.

24
00:00:50,226 --> 00:00:53,037
HTML describes the things on the page

25
00:00:53,037 --> 00:00:54,305
and their order.

26
00:00:54,305 --> 00:00:56,755
A separate style sheet describes how
they

27
00:00:56,755 --> 00:00:58,631
look and fit together.

28
00:00:58,981 --> 00:01:02,099
The postcard section contains the snail
image,

29
00:01:02,099 --> 00:01:05,007
a note, and the decorative stamp image.

30
00:01:05,007 --> 00:01:07,789
The snail's alternative text describes
it for

31
00:01:07,789 --> 00:01:09,857
someone who cannot see it.

32
00:01:10,207 --> 00:01:12,540
Open the page locally in a browser.

33
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:15,028
Here we use a small local server.

34
00:01:15,028 --> 00:01:17,463
The browser reads the HTML and its

35
00:01:17,463 --> 00:01:20,569
linked style sheet, then draws the
result.

36
00:01:20,919 --> 00:01:23,592
Without a special layout rule, blocks
normally

37
00:01:23,592 --> 00:01:25,108
follow one another.

38
00:01:25,108 --> 00:01:27,433
The note comes after the picture.

39
00:01:27,433 --> 00:01:30,229
That ordinary flow is our starting
point.

40
00:01:30,579 --> 00:01:32,231
A drag might say put the snail

41
00:01:32,231 --> 00:01:33,850
at one coordinate.

42
00:01:33,850 --> 00:01:36,236
Our author can say: put the picture

43
00:01:36,236 --> 00:01:38,275
beside the note when there is room,

44
00:01:38,275 --> 00:01:40,830
but keep both readable when there
isn't.

45
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:43,597
The postcard is the parent box.

46
00:01:43,597 --> 00:01:45,808
Its grid rule places the image and

47
00:01:45,808 --> 00:01:48,312
the note. This columns rule fits as

48
00:01:48,312 --> 00:01:50,591
many columns as it can, aiming for

49
00:01:50,591 --> 00:01:53,004
a minimum of two hundred sixty pixels

50
00:01:53,004 --> 00:01:53,616
each.

51
00:01:53,966 --> 00:01:56,169
If the available space becomes too
narrow

52
00:01:56,169 --> 00:01:58,691
for two columns, predict where the note

53
00:01:58,691 --> 00:01:59,558
will go.

54
00:01:59,908 --> 00:02:01,728
The note goes below the image.

55
00:02:01,728 --> 00:02:04,076
The browser measures the space and
keeps

56
00:02:04,076 --> 00:02:06,449
their order, using the same rule.

57
00:02:06,799 --> 00:02:08,897
The stamp has a different rule.

58
00:02:08,897 --> 00:02:11,768
The postcard is positioned relative,
making it

59
00:02:11,768 --> 00:02:13,238
a reference box.

60
00:02:13,238 --> 00:02:16,346
The stamp is positioned absolute,
outside normal

61
00:02:16,346 --> 00:02:18,580
flow, so it can overlap.

62
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:21,210
Let's move one actual picture.

63
00:02:21,210 --> 00:02:23,724
The stamp starts twelve pixels from the

64
00:02:23,724 --> 00:02:25,593
postcard's right edge.

65
00:02:25,593 --> 00:02:28,821
Change right to one hundred pixels,
save,

66
00:02:28,821 --> 00:02:29,842
and refresh.

67
00:02:30,192 --> 00:02:32,128
Here are the real browser results at

68
00:02:32,128 --> 00:02:33,453
the same width.

69
00:02:33,453 --> 00:02:35,534
The stamp moved left by eighty eight

70
00:02:35,534 --> 00:02:39,308
pixels. The postcard, snail, and note
stayed

71
00:02:39,308 --> 00:02:39,926
put.

72
00:02:40,276 --> 00:02:42,601
Narrow the browser, and the stamp stays

73
00:02:42,601 --> 00:02:45,405
one hundred pixels from the postcard's
right

74
00:02:45,405 --> 00:02:48,225
side. It can overlap the picture.

75
00:02:48,575 --> 00:02:51,335
View Source shows the original HTML
loaded

76
00:02:51,335 --> 00:02:52,522
for the page.

77
00:02:52,522 --> 00:02:55,315
Inspector shows the live document tree
and

78
00:02:55,315 --> 00:02:59,279
computed layout. Find the postcard, its
picture

79
00:02:59,279 --> 00:03:01,261
and note, and the stamp.

80
00:03:01,611 --> 00:03:04,523
Your turn. Change the stamp's right
value

81
00:03:04,523 --> 00:03:06,095
to forty pixels.

82
00:03:06,095 --> 00:03:09,497
Predict which way it moves, save,
refresh,

83
00:03:09,497 --> 00:03:12,211
and check. Then narrow the browser.

84
00:03:12,211 --> 00:03:14,257
What is the stamp attached to?

85
00:03:14,607 --> 00:03:17,066
To share the page, upload index dot

86
00:03:17,066 --> 00:03:21,384
html, style dot css, snail dot svg,

87
00:03:21,384 --> 00:03:24,551
garden dot svg, and stamp dot svg

88
00:03:24,551 --> 00:03:26,138
to a static host.

89
00:03:26,138 --> 00:03:28,636
Neocities also has a browser editor.

90
00:03:28,986 --> 00:03:31,322
A free Neocities address follows the
pattern

91
00:03:31,322 --> 00:03:34,063
site name dot neocities dot org.

92
00:03:34,063 --> 00:03:36,444
The host serves the files, and each

93
00:03:36,444 --> 00:03:38,754
visitor's browser lays them out for its

94
00:03:38,754 --> 00:03:39,837
own screen.

95
00:03:40,187 --> 00:03:43,313
The maker chose the relationships:
snail beside

96
00:03:43,313 --> 00:03:46,259
note when it fits, stamp on postcard,

97
00:03:46,259 --> 00:03:47,882
pictures in a gallery.

98
00:03:47,882 --> 00:03:49,850
The browser does the measuring.

99
00:03:49,850 --> 00:03:52,261
That's how typed instructions can make
a

100
00:03:52,261 --> 00:03:53,938
page feel handmade.
